{#- pytm's action report: what needs doing about a threat model.

    Render with:  ./tm.py --report pytm:actions.md.j2 > actions.md
    Only what needs doing: after the diagrams, the threats that apply,
    most severe first, each with how to resolve it; then the unverified
    assumptions that would suppress findings once verified, those with the
    most at stake first; then each person's list of them. Suppressed
    findings, verified assumptions and assumptions that affect no finding
    are left out, as are the element, data and threat library sections of
    the full report (pytm:report.md.j2); links to them become plain text.

    Variables (set with --report-var KEY=VALUE): dfd_image, seq_image,
    dfd_colormap and pandoc_metadata, as for report.md.j2.
-#}
{% import "_macros.md.j2" as m %}
{#- "3 findings (1 Very High, 2 High)" -#}
{% macro would_suppress(a) -%}
{{ a.pending | length }} finding{{ "s" if a.pending | length != 1 }} ({% for name, n in a.risk_counts() %}{{ n }} {{ name }}{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %})
{%- endmacro %}
{% set page_title = tm.name ~ ": Action Items" %}
{% include "sections/metadata.md.j2" %}
{% set dfd_image = dfd_image | default("dfd.png") %}
{% set seq_image = seq_image | default("seq.png") %}
{% set dfd_colormap = (dfd_colormap | default("no") | string | lower) in ("yes", "true", "1") %}
{% set groups = findings_by_severity(findings) %}
{% set to_verify = assumptions_by_risk() %}
{% filter drop_dangling_links %}
# {{ tm.name | md_escape }}: Action Items { #section-title }

What needs doing about this threat model: the threats that apply to it,
most severe first, with how to resolve each one; the unverified
assumptions that would suppress some of them once verified, those with
the most at stake first; and each person's list of assumptions to verify.

| | Count |
|---|---|
| [Findings](#section-threats-by-severity) | {{ findings | length }} |
{% for name, group in groups %}
| &nbsp;&nbsp;[{{ name }}](#section-severity-{{ name | slugify }}) | {{ group | length }} |
{% endfor %}
| [Assumptions to verify](#section-assumptions-to-verify) | {{ to_verify | length }} |
{% set people = to_verify | map(attribute="verifier") | select | unique | list %}
| [People with assumptions to verify](#section-assumptions-by-verifier) | {{ people | length }} |

{% include "sections/diagrams.md.j2" %}
## Threats by Severity { #section-threats-by-severity }

{% for name, group in groups %}
### {{ name }} ({{ group | length }}) { #section-severity-{{ name | slugify }} }

{% for f in group %}
#### Finding {{ f.id }}: {{ f.description }} {{ "{#" ~ anchor(f) ~ "}" }}

{{ m.property_table([
    ("Target", link(f.element)),
    ("Threat", f.threat_id),
    ("Severity", f.severity),
    ("Likelihood", f.likelihood),
    ("CVSS", f.cvss),
    ("Response", f.response),
]) }}

{% if f.mitigations %}
**Mitigations:** {{ f.mitigations | breakable }}

{% endif %}
{% for a in pending_assumptions_of(f) %}
**Pending verification:** {{ link(a) }} would suppress this finding once it is verified. {{ m.verification(a) }}.

{% endfor %}
{{ m.remedy_list(f) }}

{% endfor %}
{% else %}
No threats apply to this model.

{% endfor %}
## Assumptions to Verify { #section-assumptions-to-verify }

{% if not requires_verified_assumptions() %}
This model lets assumptions suppress threats before they are verified, so
none are waiting for verification here. Set
`tm.requireVerifiedAssumptions = True` to report the threats an unverified
assumption excludes as findings, and its verification as an action.

{% elif to_verify %}
Each of these assumptions excludes threats that are reported above as
findings until it is verified: if it holds, verifying it suppresses them;
if it doesn't, the findings stand. They are ordered by the combined
severity of those findings: each Very High finding counts 5, High 4,
Medium 3, Low 2 and Very Low 1.

| | Assumption | About | Responsible | Would suppress |
|-|--------|-----|-----|--------|
{% for a in to_verify %}
| {{ loop.index }} | {{ link(a) }} | {{ link(a.owner) if a.owner else "the whole model" }} | {{ a.verifier | md_escape if a.verifier else "*No one*" }} | {{ would_suppress(a) }} |
{% endfor %}

{% for a in to_verify %}
### {{ a | label | md_escape }} {{ "{#" ~ a.anchor ~ "}" }}

{% if a.description %}
{{ a.description | md_escape }}

{% endif %}
{{ m.property_table([
    ("About", link(a.owner) if a.owner else "the whole model"),
    ("Responsible", a.verifier | md_escape if a.verifier else "*No one*"),
    ("Combined severity", a.risk),
]) }}

{% set items = [] %}
{% for _name, group in findings_by_severity(a.pending) %}{% for f in group %}{% set _ = items.append("[Finding " ~ f.id ~ "](#" ~ anchor(f) ~ ") on " ~ link(f.element) ~ ": " ~ f.threat_id ~ " " ~ f.description ~ " (" ~ f.severity ~ ")") %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
{{ m.labelled_list("Would suppress", items) }}

{% endfor %}
{% else %}
None: no unverified assumption would suppress a finding.

{% endif %}
## Assumptions to Verify, by Person { #section-assumptions-by-verifier }

{% if to_verify %}
{% for person in people | sort %}
{% set theirs = to_verify | selectattr("verifier", "equalto", person) | list %}
### {{ person | md_escape }} ({{ theirs | length }})

{% for a in theirs %}
- {{ link(a) }}, about {{ link(a.owner) if a.owner else "the whole model" }}: would suppress {{ would_suppress(a) }}
{% endfor %}

{% endfor %}
{% set nobody = to_verify | rejectattr("verifier") | list %}
{% if nobody %}
### No one assigned ({{ nobody | length }})

{% for a in nobody %}
- {{ link(a) }}, about {{ link(a.owner) if a.owner else "the whole model" }}: would suppress {{ would_suppress(a) }}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% else %}
No one: there are no assumptions to verify.

{% endif %}
{% endfilter %}
